# docker/ diverges too, in two files, and both are deliberate.
# docker/crontab runs at 02:00 rather than the template's 07:00, and
# docker/entrypoint.sh drops the block that copies config.example.json
# when no config.json is present: a container here must fail loudly
# rather than quietly publish somebody else's pools. Resolve a conflict
# in either by keeping this side.
#
# README.md diverges from the template on purpose: this repository's
# entry point describes the instance, not the software, and the template's
# own README is a manual for building a different site. A template merge
# that touches it conflicts; resolve by keeping this side and porting
# anything genuinely new by hand. docs/ is inherited unchanged and merges
# cleanly.
#
# This repository is the published instance, so it does NOT inherit the
# template's "instance data" block. Everything the template ignores as
# generated output (history.json, the feeds, index.html, archive.html,
# archive-*.html, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, 404.html, birds/, assets/,
# cache/, maps/) is exactly what this repository exists to publish, and
# the daily workflow stages it with "git add -A .". Adding those lines
# here would silently stop new pages from ever being committed.

# Agent scratch (worktrees and plan ledgers, never published)
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
